---
// The animated fire mark. Currently the glyph inside Retrospective's
// "Thanks for Scrolling" ring, replacing the static conifer that sat there
// (which the icon set carries under the `smile` key — the key is named for
// the slot, not for the drawing).
//
// 24 baked drawings swapped with CSS `steps()`. No Lottie, no player, no JS.
// That is the whole reason this exists as SVG rather than as a Lottie export
// like AnimatedLogo: Lottie bakes its fill colors at export time and can't
// follow a CSS custom property, so the logo needs one JSON per theme
// (max-logo.json + max-logo-light.json, see AnimatedLogo's header). Every
// frame here is `fill="currentColor"`, so the mark inherits whatever its
// container sets and inverts across themes on its own, one asset.
//
// Provenance — the frames are auto-traced from a reference GIF Max supplied,
// `fire-reference.gif`. **That source is deliberately NOT in the repo** (6.8MB,
// untracked and gitignored under uploads/), and neither is the tracing
// pipeline, which was scratch-only. So these frames are effectively not
// reproducible from this repository alone: changing the mark means re-tracing
// from Max's copy of the GIF, rebuilding threshold detection, contour tracing,
// corner-aware smoothing and the seamless-subloop search. The two numbers
// below are recorded precisely because they are the part that would otherwise
// be lost, and both were got wrong first:
//   - Threshold 100. The source's luminance histogram is bimodal with a dead
//     zone between 72 and 111; 100 sits in that valley and traces the flame.
//     Cutting lower traces the GLOW HALO around the flame instead, which
//     comes out a featureless pear — that was the first attempt.
//   - Frames 73-96 of the 144-frame source. Consecutive frames in that clip
//     overlap at a median IoU of 0.9125, so any pair matching at least that
//     well is by definition an invisible cut; 73 against 97 matches at
//     0.9326, tighter than an average frame step. The excerpt is exactly 24
//     frames, so it lands on a 1.00s loop at a sixth of the path data, and it
//     still contains one spark detachment.
//
// Holds down to about 32px; below that the side notches and the detached
// spark stop registering and it reads as a plain blob. 34 is Max's call for
// the ring, sized against the real circle-doodle rather than in isolation —
// an earlier note here claimed a ~40px floor and a 48 default, which was
// measured for reading the notches on their own and was contradicted by the
// only real usage.
import { FLAME_FRAMES, FLAME_FPS } from './frames';

interface Props {
  /** Rendered box in px. Default 34; see the legibility floor above. */
  size?: number;
  class?: string;
}

const { size = 34, class: className } = Astro.props;

// The @keyframes below hardcodes its cutoff for a 24-frame loop. Percentage
// keyframe selectors reject calc() and var(), so that window genuinely cannot
// be derived from the frame count at runtime — fail loudly rather than
// silently desync if the trace is ever regenerated at a different length.
if (FLAME_FRAMES.length !== 24) {
  const slot = 100 / FLAME_FRAMES.length;
  throw new Error(
    `AnimatedFlame: the keyframes assume 24 frames, got ${FLAME_FRAMES.length}. ` +
      `Update the @keyframes cutoff to just under ${slot.toFixed(4)}% too — see the ` +
      `comment there for why it must not be exactly one slot.`,
  );
}

const duration = FLAME_FRAMES.length / FLAME_FPS;
---

<svg
  class:list={['animated-flame', className]}
  width={size}
  height={size}
  viewBox="0 0 28 28"
  aria-hidden="true"
  style={`--flame-dur:${duration}s;--flame-n:${FLAME_FRAMES.length}`}
>
  {
    FLAME_FRAMES.map((d, i) => (
      <g class="animated-flame__frame" style={`--flame-i:${i}`}>
        <path d={d} fill="currentColor" />
      </g>
    ))
  }
</svg>

<style>
  /* No `color` declared here on purpose, same reasoning Icon.astro's header
     spells out: a consumer passing `class="foo"` merges onto this SAME
     element, so an explicit `color` here would tie in specificity with their
     own rule and the winner would depend on stylesheet bundling order
     (bug-002). Omitting it leaves exactly one real `color` declaration in
     play — the container's. */
  /* overflow: visible because the trace fitted the viewBox to the flame's
     BODY on purpose — including the detached spark in the fit inflated the
     box and shrank the flame ~9% inside its own frame. The cost of that
     choice is that the spark reaches about 1 unit past the top of the box on
     frames 14 and 15, and an SVG root clips to its viewport by default, so
     without this those two frames rendered with the spark cut off flat.
     Note for future callers: the spark can therefore paint just outside this
     element's box. Free in a 128px ring with ~45px of clear space above it,
     not free in a tight container. */
  .animated-flame {
    display: block;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    overflow: visible;
  }
  /* Each frame is opaque for exactly one slot of the cycle, offset by its
     index. A literal duration, not a token: tokens.css's durations are all
     sub-second UI transitions and none fits a multi-second decorative loop —
     same precedent as Retrospective's own 45s ring spin. */
  .animated-flame__frame {
    opacity: 0;
    animation: animated-flame-swap var(--flame-dur) steps(1, end) infinite;
    animation-delay: calc(var(--flame-dur) * var(--flame-i) / var(--flame-n));
  }
  /* 4.1666%, deliberately a hair under one slot's 100/24 = 4.1667%. At exactly
     the slot boundary `steps(1, end)` resolves the outgoing frame as still
     visible while the incoming one is already visible, so two drawings paint
     stacked and the mark visibly thickens. That is not a rounding curiosity:
     41.667ms slots and 16.667ms paints align every 83.3ms, so it hit 11 of
     every 60 painted frames (measured). Trimming the window by 0.7µs makes the
     intervals disjoint — the gap is far too small for a paint to land in, and
     the aligned boundaries now resolve to exactly one frame. */
  @keyframes animated-flame-swap {
    0% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    4.1666% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
    100% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }
  /* Frame 0 is a legitimate drawing of the flame at rest, so it stands in as
     the still frame directly — unlike the stroked variant, this mark has no
     separate static original to fall back to. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .animated-flame__frame {
      animation: none;
      opacity: 0;
    }
    .animated-flame__frame:first-of-type {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
